# CSS Variables for Theming

Using CSS custom properties defined in MARP frontmatter to create consistent, easily changeable color schemes across presentation slides.

## Implementation

Defined within the `style:` block of MARP frontmatter:

```css
:root {
  --color-primary: #5b8ff9;
  --color-secondary: #61ddaa;
  --color-accent: #f6bd16;
  --color-warm: #f76b6b;
  --color-cool: #5d7092;
}
```

## Best Practices
- Use CSS variables for colors (easy to change theme)
- Define highlight boxes with gradients using variables
- Set consistent fonts and spacing
- Avoid external stylesheets for portability

## Highlight Box Styles
```css
.highlight {
  padding: 1rem;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(91, 143, 249, 0.1), rgba(97, 221, 170, 0.1));
  border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
  border-radius: 4px;
}
```

